*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* XAPROBE  -  WHICH ESA/390 MNEMONICS DOES CE'S ASSEMBLER XF KNOW?    *
*                                                                     *
* XAOPS EXISTS BECAUSE CE'S ASSEMBLER PREDATES 370-XA.  THAT RAISES A *
* QUESTION XAOPS CANNOT ANSWER: IS THE LIST COMPLETE?  GUESSING WHICH *
* MNEMONICS A 1970S ASSEMBLER KNOWS IS EXACTLY THE KIND OF ASSUMPTION *
* THIS PROJECT HAS BEEN WRONG ABOUT BEFORE, SO THIS FILE MEASURES IT  *
* INSTEAD.  EVERY CANDIDATE APPEARS AS A NATIVE MNEMONIC; WHATEVER    *
* THE ASSEMBLER FLAGS IS THE GAP, AND NOTHING ELSE IS.                *
*                                                                     *
* RUN WITH NO MACLIB GLOBAL AT ALL:                                   *
*                                                                     *
*   GLOBAL MACLIB                                                     *
*   ASSEMBLE XAPROBE (DISK                                            *
*                                                                     *
* CLEARING THE GLOBAL LIST MATTERS.  WITH XALIB ACTIVE, A NAME THAT   *
* HAPPENS TO MATCH A MACRO WOULD RESOLVE QUIETLY AND LOOK LIKE AN     *
* INSTRUCTION THE ASSEMBLER KNOWS -- THE SAME CONFUSION THAT MADE THE *
* FIRST Z390 VALIDATION WORTHLESS.                                    *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         PRINT GEN,DATA
XAPROBE  CSECT
R0       EQU   0
R1       EQU   1
R2       EQU   2
R4       EQU   4
R14      EQU   14
R15      EQU   15
         BALR  R15,0
         USING *,R15
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* GROUP 1 -- CONTROLS.  EVERY ONE OF THESE IS S/370 AND MUST BE       *
* ACCEPTED.  IF ANY IS FLAGGED THEN THE PROBE ITSELF IS BROKEN AND    *
* THE REST OF THE RESULT MEANS NOTHING.                               *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LRA   R1,0(0,R2)
         ISK   R1,R2
         SSK   R1,R2
         RRB   0(R2)
         LCTL  R1,R1,WORD
         STCTL R0,R0,WORD
         STOSM BYTE,X'04'
         STNSM BYTE,X'FB'
         STIDP DWORD
         STIDC WORD
         CS    R1,R2,WORD
         STCK  DWORD
         SPX   WORD
         STPX  WORD
         STAP  HWORD
         SIGP  R0,R1,0(R2)
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* GROUP 2 -- ESA/390 DAT.  M2 NEEDS THESE.                            *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         PTLB
         IPTE  R1,R2
         IVSK  R1,R2
         TPROT 0(R1),0(R2)
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* GROUP 3 -- ESA/390 4 KB STORAGE KEYS.  R-12 NEEDS THESE, BECAUSE A  *
* GUEST READING ITS OWN KEYS THROUGH ISK EXPECTS 2 KB SEMANTICS AND   *
* DMKPRV HAS TO BRIDGE THAT.                                          *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         ISKE  R1,R2
         SSKE  R1,R2
         RRBE  R1,R2
         TB    R1,R2
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* GROUP 4 -- THE REST OF THE CHANNEL-SUBSYSTEM BLOCK.  XAOPS STOPS AT *
* B239; B23A THROUGH B23C ARE CHANNEL-PATH AND MONITOR CONTROL, WHICH *
* THE CHANNEL-LOGOUT REWRITE (R-03) MAY WANT.                         *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         RCHP
         STCPS WORD
         SCHM
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* GROUP 5 -- INFORMATIONAL, NOT REQUIRED.  IF XF KNOWS ANY OF THESE   *
* THE CONVERSION CODE CAN BE WRITTEN MORE CLEANLY -- RELATIVE         *
* BRANCHES AND HALFWORD IMMEDIATES WOULD REMOVE A LOT OF LITERAL AND  *
* BASE-REGISTER FIDDLING FROM NEW CODE.  NOTHING DEPENDS ON THEM.     *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
         LHI   R1,1
         AHI   R1,1
         CHI   R1,1
         MHI   R1,1
         BRAS  R14,BRTGT
         BRC   15,BRTGT
BRTGT    DS    0H
         MVST  R1,R2
         CLST  R1,R2
         SRST  R1,R2
         CUSE  R2,R4
         LURA  R1,R2
         STURA R1,R2
         STCKE DWORD16
         TRACE R0,R1,WORD
*
         BR    R14
*
         DS    0F
WORD     DS    F
HWORD    DS    H
BYTE     DS    X
         DS    0D
DWORD    DS    D
DWORD16  DS    2D
         LTORG
         END
